      <title>Squeak 2.23.38</title>
      <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:39:03 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22338</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.23.38</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Chat tabs fit their name: the close button sits right after the title instead of at the far edge.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.37</h4><ul><li>A pond can be any folder, git or not. Chats run right in the folder; things that need version history (streams, changes, pull requests) step aside and say why, and "Turn on version history" in the pond's settings sets it up when you want it.</li><li>Clean up disk: a page (Settings › General, or a pond's menu) lists stream folders Squeak no longer tracks, stale worktrees and merged branches with their sizes. Safe items are ticked, anything with unsaved work never is, and folders go to the Trash.</li><li>Archiving a stream whose branch is merged offers to delete the branch.</li><li>Settings › Add-ons: an action spins and fails only on its own card, gives up after 15 seconds with a reason, Remove on Zoho Cliq really removes it, and add-ons that aren't in this build don't offer Add.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.36</h4><ul><li>Updating while agents work is safe and says so: the update row tells you your chats keep working, Install asks first only if a terminal tab is running something (Install when free, Install now, Cancel), and drafts are kept across the restart.</li><li>The agent engine catches up on its own: an engine update that had to wait for running chats now installs as soon as they finish, or right away with Restart now.</li><li>The window controls sit in line with the duck in a normal window, as they do in full screen.</li><li>Squeak no longer ships Anthropic's agent kit inside the app: it downloads the exact published version from npm the first time it's needed and checks it before use.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
